# ocp.env — OpenShift Router broker site (Option A: no AWS, no custom domain)
#
# In OCP broker mode the session broker is a Route on the cluster itself and
# audience instances are reached directly at their own `audience` Route. There
# is no separate public domain fronting them, so BROKER_DOMAIN is simply the
# cluster's apps domain — which makes the "public" host that
# post-restart-repatch.sh derives resolve to the same hostname as the audience
# Route, and lets demo-preflight.sh's broker-origin check match it.
#
# Use with:
#   ./post-restart-repatch.sh --site ocp 1 22
#   ./demo-preflight.sh --site ocp 1 22
#
# BROKER_S3_BUCKET / ALB_NAME / TG_NAME / HAPROXY_SG_NAME / IAM_ROLE_NAME are
# deliberately left unset: they only apply to the S3 + ALB + HAProxy broker, and
# resolve-site.sh will fill in the primary site's defaults for them. Nothing in
# the OCP path reads those values.
#
# BROKER_DOMAIN is cluster-specific — update it when pointing at a new cluster.
SITE_NAME=ocp
BROKER_DOMAIN=apps.cluster-jzsjx.dyn.redhatworkshops.io
